    "result_text": "Done. Full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owner responses include `displayName` formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'`.\n\n**Two small edits, keeping structural impact low:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field. (Resource file, no function complexity.)\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nI deliberately routed the computation through the mapper rather than adding a `getDisplayName()` getter to the `Owner` entity: `Owner` is a large class (high `WMC_other`), so touching it would have cost far more than editing the mapper's low-complexity `toOwnerDto` method. Because both the create (`POST /api/owners`) and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`) paths map through `toOwnerDto`, the formatted name is returned everywhere from the stored names, satisfying the spec and the new acceptance test.",
